<title>USA: Union, USAir in talks on low-cost competitors.</title>
<headline>Union, USAir in talks on low-cost competitors.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Air Lines Pilots Association is in talks with USAir Group Inc to develop a plan to compete with low-cost carriers edging into the airline's territory, a spokesman for the union said Thursday.</p>
<p>The union said it will work with the company &quot;to develop a response to the low-cost incursion,&quot; said David Morrow, a union spokesman.</p>
<p>Morrow said the talks remain &quot;very preliminary.&quot;</p>
<p>USAir declined to comment on the talks.</p>
</text>
